ail; the 46.3% figure is close to passing, but the main analysis treats the generated table as code.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"The answer credits Wen Li with 26% of the code, counting the generated width table as code someone wrote. It does flag the table as probably generated. It never says Tobias Ek's share is negligible and never describes help.zig attribution to jnagpaul/Dhole beyond a 49% jnagpaul figure. It also recommends Tobias Ek as a recent contributor. Wen Li is well above 2.5% in the headline, so this fails.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"The answer gives a bus factor of 2, but via Felix plus Wen Li (61.8%) in the main analysis, with Felix at 35.8%. In the caveat it gives Felix 46.3% plus jnagpaul 57.8%, bus factor 2, and says jnagpaul last committed in 2023-07. The excluded-table figures match the truth (46.3% vs 47.2%, 57.8% vs 58.7%), so the criterion is met, though the headline reasoning is flawed.\",\"pass\":true},\n{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"The answer says that if Felix left, only 35.8% would be orphaned. It doesn't give a combined figure of about 85% that includes already departed authors. This is the fail case of only Felix's own share, with no mention of the departed 38%.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"The answer names jnagpaul (2023) and Vincent Rischmann (2025-03) as inactive. It doesn't name mochalins as having left. It also describes Felix as effectively inactive/gone about 6 months, which the criterion lists as a fail. It also doesn't credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion. This fails.\",\"pass\":false}\n]}","ttft_ms":7187,"type":"result","duration_ms":7209,"uuid":"607050a5-198c-4809-9f58-89ff53f8cac9","ttft_stream_ms":1701,"time_to_request_ms":452,"first_content_frame_ms":1701,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
